QUIC test certificates are generated on demand — run gen.sh in this
directory (the CMake configure step does this automatically when
PAHO_WITH_QUIC is enabled and the certificates are missing).

Do not commit the generated *.pem files; they are git-ignored.

Generated files:
- cacert.pem / cakey.pem — test CA
- cert.pem / key.pem — server certificate (CN=localhost)
- client-cert.pem / client-key.pem — client certificate
- untrusted-cacert.pem / untrusted-cakey.pem — second CA used by the
  EMQX :18887 listener so the server cannot verify the test client cert
  (test9000-2b)

Broker packet-size notes for test9000-7 / test7:
- Local EMQX (`test/emqx.conf`) sets `mqtt.max_packet_size = 100MB`, so
  the default 5 MB payload is appropriate in CI.
- Tencent TDMQ documents a 4 MB maximum MQTT packet.  When pointing
  test9000 at TDMQ, pass `--size 2097152` (2 MB).  A 4–5 MB failure
  against TDMQ is a broker limit, not a client write-path defect.
